  "description": "The back of the neck and the shoulders. Below the occiput, the depression between sternocleidomastoid and trapezius overlies the suboccipital muscles; deep and medial to it lie the vertebral arteries on the atlas and, in the midline below the foramen magnum, the medulla. On the top of the shoulder, between C7 and the acromion, trapezius and supraspinatus overlie the apex of the lung and its pleura, which in a slim adult may be only a few centimetres below the skin. In the midline below C7 the supraspinous and interspinous ligaments lead to the spinal canal.",
